.TH WERKMEISTER-CONFIG 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-config \- Set up and maintain the machine\-global werkmeister config (~/.werkmeister/config.yaml — the single source of truth); regenerates env.sh and wires up ~/.zshenv and the Desktop MCP config
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister config\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-write\fR
Write config.yaml (prompting on a TTY for unset values), regenerate env.sh, and wire up ~/.zshenv and the Desktop MCP config. Without it (or a value to set) the command only prints the config.
.TP
\fB\-\-repos\-root <path>\fR
Absolute path to the canonical source\-repo clones (non\-interactive set).
.TP
\fB\-\-workspaces\-root <path>\fR
Absolute path to the per\-feature worktree workspaces (non\-interactive set).
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR
Print the resolved config and each value's origin (the default).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Validate config + derived files; nonzero exit on drift.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Sets up and maintains the machine\-global configuration, \fB~/.werkmeister/config.yaml\fR, the single source of truth. Writing it also regenerates \fB~/.werkmeister/env.sh\fR and keeps a managed block in \fB~/.zshenv\fR that sources it. The \fBWERKMEISTER_*\fR environment variables are derived from the YAML, not read as input.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister config                       # print the resolved config and origins
werkmeister config \-\-write               # interactive wizard, then write
werkmeister config \-\-check               # validate; nonzero exit on drift
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
